bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 0, "When a spec imports two classes with the same bare name from different modules (plugins.backend_cuda.cuda_backend.CudaBackend and compiler.backend.backend.cuda_backend.CudaBackend as LegacyCudaBackend), self-method calls made inside the plugin object's compile() run the LEGACY class's methods. Repro: cuda_backend_intensive_contract_spec 'pads mixed width tuple GEP strides' emitted GEP stride 10 (legacy unpadded tuple size) while a direct backend.cuda_type_size call on the same object returned 24; removing the legacy import made it, and 3 fail-closed layout examples, pass. Distinct from the type-resolution case cross_module_class_name_collision_resolution_2026-08-17 (marked fixed)."

