bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 5, "2026-11-27 Fable re-review fixes: a bare identity of a shared class name matches a pattern/type only when the executing scope resolves the name to the bare class (entry P no longer matches qa.P: main_entry_neg a_entry 9 -> -1; red on 5c1578ed272, body spec 6/7 -> 7/7); negative cases added (qa_any(qb_make()) = -1, alias rejection, entry case) to the body spec and 3 Rust tests (16/16); overload owner-scope scan gated on a monotonic renamed-class flag; method-not-found and HIR Cannot-infer-field-type messages print the source name; the co-compiled class warning is restored (JIT patterns still ignore owner). JIT pattern gap (t1/t2/t4 JIT), wrong-owner overload fallthrough (t7b) and the no-scope fail-open filed as separate shards. Full suite: same 53 failing tests; spec slice vs base unchanged apart from the new specs and cuda 33->36. Perf 3 alternated rounds: microbench interp 1.93-1.95 vs 1.92-1.95s, big probe interp 1.56-1.68 vs 1.32-1.94s, jit 3.31-5.82 vs 3.25-3.58s, RSS within 5%."
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 4, "2026-11-27 Fable review fixes: owner-exact instances matched by class_identity_matches (struct pattern, typed match / matches_type, constructor-param scoring) resolving the type name through the executing module scope; overload scoring runs in the candidate module scope; mangled names stripped from unknown-static / no-overload / unknown-class / no-field errors; identifier hooks check the collision flag before env.is_local. Red on 865e7bb6d37: same_name_class_body_identity_spec 2/4 (struct + generic Box<T> patterns returned -1 in the interpreter; JIT already matched); green 4/4, Rust same_name_class_owner_identity 13/13. Same-module overload case was green before and after (guard only). Full simple-compiler suite: same 53 failing tests as the previous head run (all pre-existing or an order flake). Spec slice (192 specs) vs base: only the 3 new specs and cuda 33->36 differ. Perf base vs head, 3 alternated rounds, collision present: method microbench interp 1.93-1.94 vs 1.94-1.97s, jit 0.03-0.04 both; 18k-item flattened probe interp 1.38-1.62 vs 1.41-1.48s, jit 3.30-3.45 vs 3.36-3.60s; RSS equal. Enum names stay out of the interpreter census on purpose (owner-keyed enum tables), HIR still renames differing-layout enums."
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 3, "2026-11-27 follow-up: fixtures gain trait Labeled (impl in pa/pb); TRAIT_IMPLS keyed by owner identity; JIT struct display keeps the owner symbol for FieldGet (vtable offset; was printing pointers). New same_name_class_mixed_lane_spec (flattened pa + lazy pb alias + trait) red on base (duplicate impl error), green on head. Spec slice test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter (189 specs) + cuda spec, SIMPLE_TEST_DAEMON_CHILD=1, base vs head: only diffs are the two new specs and cuda 33->36. Large flattened collision probe (plugin+legacy CudaBackend single imports, ~18k items) JIT strict OK both, min-of-3 jit 3.60 vs 3.67s, interp 1.44 vs 1.48s (box noise > 2%), RSS equal (1.26-1.31 GB / 0.67 GB). Follow-up filed: interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27."
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 2, "2026-11-27 opus-same-name-class fix (owner decision: class identity = owner module; no refusal policy). Flattened lane: flatten_struct_owner census treats every distinct-owner struct/class name as a collision and renames ALL owned declarations to flatten_owner_mangled_name; the interpreter (evaluate_module_items) applies the same qualify_items_in_place; aliases (use m.{Thing as Legacy}), namespace (pb.Thing) and type aliases resolve through the owner scope. Lazy lane (test runner load_and_merge_module): the second owner of a class name registers under the owner-exact symbol (lazy_class_identity), importers merge it via class_slot_key, resolve_class_for_instance matches identities exactly. Red->green: tests/same_name_class_owner_identity.rs 0/10 -> 10/10 (interp+JIT: alias, braced alias, namespace, third-module alias, entry-own); test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_owner_identity_spec.spl 0/5 -> 5/5; cuda_backend_intensive_contract_spec 33/38 -> 36/38 (the 3 tracked examples green; remaining 2 fail on base too). Microbench sum base 9600000 (wrong class) head 206800000 (correct), interp 1.91-2.02s vs 1.92-1.94s, RSS equal; cuda spec RSS ~850MB both (direct run). Full simple-compiler suite: no new failures vs base f43f68c218e. Remaining gap: entry module importing two LAZILY loaded same-named classes still errors ambiguous type (entry has no owner bindings; pre-existing, loud). Pure-Simple compiler filed: pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27."
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch triage (not claimed): minimal repro on seed c6f98def228712ea aarch64, release/1.0.0 25308aa2aed. pa/thing.spl and pb/thing.spl each define class Thing (create/size/compile differ); main imports pa Thing and pb Thing as Legacy. Interpreter AND JIT (0 fallbacks) print ln=1 lsize=24 b.compile=24 (expected 2, 10, 1010): Legacy.create() itself resolves to pa, so it is wider than the filed self-call shape. pipeline/module_loader.rs:2283 already warns that the flattened class registry is keyed on the bare name. Fix needs re-keying classes by owner module across the flatten for interpreter and JIT, or a mangle-vs-error policy for classes like the 2026-11-09 one for functions: owner decision, left open."
    interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26, 0, "2026-11-26 seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-wr-seed1126b/release/simple, aarch64: with the legacy import the spec fails 'rejects an unresolved struct field', 'rejects unresolved aggregate construction writes and GEP', 'rejects missing nested wrong kind and cyclic by value layouts'; a copy without the legacy import passes all three. Exact dispatch site not yet located (file column is a candidate, not a diagnosis)."

